    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Beautifully Upgraded Coastal Home Just Moments from Bray Seafront\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned only 250 metres from Bray Beach, this beautifully presented detached residence offers an exceptional opportunity to enjoy coastal living at its finest. Located just a short stroll from the vibrant Bray Promenade, the famous Bray Head Walk, cafés, restaurants and a host of local amenities, this impressive home seamlessly combines original 1930s character with thoughtfully modernised interiors.\r\n\r\nSince purchasing the property, the current owners have undertaken an extensive programme of upgrades including rewiring, new heating system, new boiler, replacement front door, improved insulation, a luxurious new en-suite bathroom, new flooring throughout and complete redecoration, creating a home that is both stylish and energy efficient while retaining its original charm.\r\n\r\nOffering spacious and versatile accommodation throughout, the property enjoys bright dual-aspect rooms, high ceilings, original period features, generous off-street parking and wonderfully private mature gardens.\r\n\r\nBray is one of County Wicklow's most sought-after coastal towns, renowned for its stunning seaside setting, excellent amenities and strong transport links. The town offers an exceptional range of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools and sporting facilities, while the nearby Bray Head and Cliff Walk provide some of the most scenic walking routes on the east coast. Frequent DART and Dublin Bus services provide easy access to Dublin City Centre, making Bray an ideal location for those seeking a balance between coastal living and city convenience.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThe property is approached via a pedestrian entrance with steps leading through a beautifully landscaped front garden featuring mature trees, colourful planting, established shrubbery and attractive solar lighting.\r\n\r\nA separate gated vehicular entrance leads to an exceptionally spacious driveway providing parking for up to 3/4 cars. The mature gardens are a particular feature of the property, with established hedging, colourful planting and magnificent mature trees creating a wonderful sense of privacy and tranquillity.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is laid mainly in lawn, bordered by fencing and mature planting, and enjoys a high degree of privacy. A generous timber deck provides an ideal setting for outdoor entertaining, while a separate seating area offers the perfect place to relax and enjoy the peaceful surroundings.\r\nThe property is fully double glazed throughout.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway\r\nA welcoming entrance hallway accessed via a modern UPVC front door. The hallway immediately impresses with its excellent ceiling height, decorative ceiling coving, recessed lighting and attractive original 1930s doors, creating a bright and inviting first impression. A decorative archway further enhances the character of this elegant space.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nSituated to the front of the property, this charming reception room enjoys a bright dual aspect and features an attractive open fireplace with marble hearth, timber mantelpiece and surround, creating a warm focal point for the room.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nLocated to the front of the property, this spacious double bedroom enjoys a dual aspect with delightful sea views. Complete with built-in wardrobes and an original 1930s door, this room is filled with natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\nA generous double bedroom overlooking the side garden with built-in wardrobes and ample space for additional bedroom furniture.\r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom\r\nA spacious rear-facing double bedroom with built-in wardrobes and elegant French doors opening directly onto the rear patio, creating a seamless connection with the garden. An original door leads to the luxurious ensuite bathroom.\r\n\r\nEnsuite\r\nRecently upgraded to a high standard, the ensuite comprises a large walk-in shower with rainfall shower head and separate handheld attachment, WC, wash hand basin with vanity storage unit, illuminated wall mirror, chrome heated towel rail, fully tiled walls and floor, and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\r\nThe family bathroom is well appointed and comprises a bath with overhead shower attachment, WC, wash hand basin with vanity storage, illuminated wall mirror, heated towel rail and fully tiled walls and flooring.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining / Family Room\r\nA superb open-plan living space designed for modern family life. The dining and family area features attractive timber flooring, decorative ceiling coving, a feature solid fuel stove with decorative brick surround, marble hearth and timber mantelpiece, together with a useful understairs storage cupboard housing the recently installed boiler and hot water tank.\r\n\r\nThe bright dual-aspect kitchen overlooks the side and rear gardens and is fitted with an extensive range of wall and floor units finished with marble worktops. Integrated appliances include a Samsung hob, Electrolux double oven, Candy microwave and integrated dishwasher, while recessed lighting completes this stylish and functional space.\r\n\r\nConservatory\r\nLocated off the kitchen, the conservatory enjoys tiled flooring and sliding patio doors opening directly onto the driveway and gardens, providing an excellent additional reception area with easy access for indoor-outdoor living.\r\n\r\nSpecial Features\r\nPrime coastal location just 250 metres from Bray Beach with Sea Views\r\nOnly a short walk to Bray Promenade and Bray Head\r\nBeautifully upgraded throughout by the current owners\r\nNew high-efficiency boiler\r\nGas fired central heating\r\nNew double-glazed windows and upgraded front door\r\nStylish new en-suite bathroom\r\nExcellent insulation upgrades for improved energy efficiency\r\nBright dual-aspect accommodation with high ceilings and original 1930s features\r\nSpacious driveway with off-street parking for up to five cars\r\nExceptionally private mature gardens with decking, seating area and magnificent established trees"
      },
